    "updated_at": "2017-03-31T01:57:10Z",
    "body": "No, they're somewhat orthogonal.  This issue is specifically about the case when the parent `<iframe>` has a `marginwidth` but no `marginheight` or vice versa, and not about how those get ordered with the other attributes involved.\r\n\r\nI guess we could have a broader \"figure out what browsers actually do with this stuff in general\" issue if we want.  That gets us into some pretty weird behavior, though (e.g.  WebKit doesn't even handle dynamic changes to the `<iframe>`'s attributes...)",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
