    "updated_at": "2017-03-31T09:56:48Z",
    "body": "Searching httparchive for iframe with marginwidth but not marginheight and filtering out those containing `display:none` or `amazon-adsystem.com` leaves 458 matches (out of ~500,000 pages). I analyzed the first 20 matches and found only 1 with a visual difference (either rendering seems acceptable):\r\n\r\nhttp://www.navinside.com/\r\nAn ad on the right hand side:\r\n```\r\n<iframe name=\"foot_banner\" src=\"./banner_main_right.php\" scrolling=\"no\" bgcolor=\"white\" marginwidth=\"0\" width=\"190\" height=\"610\" frameborder=\"0\"></iframe>\r\n```\r\nDocument inside is in quirks mode. Firefox has 0 top margin, Chromium/WebKit 8px.\r\n\r\nThe other matches either have changed and no longer use such an iframe or they specify `marginheight` on the `<body>` or set margin to 0 with CSS.\r\n\r\nSo it seems there are no strong web compat constraints for this issue.",
