    "created_at": "2020-04-20T13:46:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-04-20T13:46:56Z",
    "body": "> Do you think we can remove support for the iframe/frame attributes entirely?\r\n\r\nThis would get rid of the communication channel completely and be easier to understand for web developers. However, it would likely regress rendering of more pages. If my earlier analysis of pages using only marginwidth is representative of all pages, only 1 of 20 pages using these attributes actually have an effect. That means the breakage would be:\r\n\r\n* remove feature: 0.1% of pages would get **8px** margin instead of what they specified (98.5% specify 0)\r\n* above proposal: 0.0015% of pages would get **0px** margin instead of what they specified",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
